title: Ribbon
---
Cat: Oh…? 

Cat: And what have we here… a ribbon once belonging to the girl in blue?

Lorina: I found it by the queen’s entrance. I know that the queen took her, but the gate is locked. How do I get in?

Cat: Mm... yes, as doors tend to do when one wishes them open.

Cat: By chance, have you tried…unlocking it?

Lorina: Listen, I'm trying to save my sister. I don't have time for this!

Cat: No, you don't, and I suppose she doesn't either

Lorina: ...

Cat: And yet, here you are asking silly questions instead of getting answers.

Lorina: Then stop talking in circles and help me!

Cat: Help you?

Cat: You’re quick to assume that I haven't been doing that this entire time?

Lorina: Then say something useful, please?

Cat: Useful?

Cat: Is that not what I’ve been doing this whole time?

Cat: You’ve already found what she left behind, but not what she lost.

Lorina: What does that even mean?!
Cat: It means you are still looking at the world only from your perspective.
Cat: Sometimes to find the truth, you need to grow and shrink, and push things into existence.

